																	"target": {
																		"$ref": "AAAAAAFkBNWq6uSUtVY="
																	},
																	"visibility": "public"
																}
															],
															"documentation": "Fragments are the structures that support a page's contents. They define the elements to be included on the header section and the\ndata providers that should generate any list of data to be rendered on the body of the page. All those pages share the same structure.\nA fixed header and an scrollable content list. Just the data source will make each page different from each other.\nAlso each page defines som elements of the ActionBar. The title and the subtitle are mandatory but fragments can adapt to other\nActionBar structures if the Activity demands that specialization.\n@author Adam Antinoo",
															"visibility": "public",
